{"arguments": null, "input": "const p = await tools.update_plan({plan:[\n  {step:\"Inspect prompt, translator subset, and reference K semantics\",status:\"in_progress\"},\n  {step:\"Implement solution.py and generate solution.mpy\",status:\"pending\"},\n  {step:\"Write verification.k, spec.k, and prove.sh\",status:\"pending\"},\n  {step:\"Compile, exercise with krun, and close all kprove claims\",status:\"pending\"},\n  {step:\"Audit deliverables and report exact result\",status:\"pending\"}\n]});\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"pwd && rg --files -g 'prompt.py' -g 'py2mpy.py' -g 'reference-semantics/**' -g 'AGENTS.md' | sort && sed -n '1,240p' prompt.py && sed -n '1,280p' py2mpy.py\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:30000});\ntext(r.output);", "line": 14, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
{"arguments": null, "input": "const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '281,700p' py2mpy.py && sed -n '1,280p' reference-semantics/semantics.k && sed -n '1,260p' reference-semantics/semantics/core.k && sed -n '1,240p' reference-semantics/semantics/int.k && sed -n '1,240p' reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k && sed -n '1,220p' reference-semantics/semantics/controls.k\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:50000});\ntext(r.output);", "line": 18, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
{"arguments": null, "input": null, "line": 24, "message": "The target is Euclid\u2019s algorithm. I\u2019m normalizing both inputs with `abs` so the implementation covers all integers (including negative inputs) and returns the conventional nonnegative gcd; the main proof obligation will be universal rather than just replaying the two examples. The key technical point is expressing the loop invariant in a form the supplied semantics and SMT backend can discharge without altering the reference files.", "name": null, "phase": "commentary", "type": "agent_message"}
{"arguments": null, "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/solution.py\\n+def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\\n+    a = abs(a)\\n+    b = abs(b)\\n+    while b != 0:\\n+        remainder = a % b\\n+        a = b\\n+        b = remainder\\n+    return a\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst a = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\\npython3 -m py_compile solution.py\\nsed -n '1,200p' solution.mpy\\nkompile --version\\nkrun --version\\nkprove --version\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:20000});\ntext(a);\ntext(r.output);", "line": 26, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
