{"arguments": null, "input": null, "line": 195, "message": "The first symbolic attempt exposed two real proof-engineering issues rather than a program bug: unconstrained frame maps caused irrelevant closure-cell branches, and the backend does not automatically derive Euclid\u2019s divisibility lemma through nested modulo terms. I\u2019ve eliminated the spurious state branches; I\u2019m now isolating the arithmetic lemma so it is either proved once and reused or replaced by an explicit executable gcd specification, rather than silently assuming it in the program theorem.", "name": null, "phase": "commentary", "type": "agent_message"}
{"arguments": null, "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/arith_spec.k\\n+requires \\\"verification.k\\\"\\n+\\n+module ARITH-SPEC\\n+  imports GCD-VERIFICATION\\n+\\n+  claim <k> commonDivisor(D:Int, B:Int, pyMod(A:Int, B)) => true </k>\\n+    requires A >=Int 0 andBool B >Int 0 andBool D >=Int 0\\n+      andBool commonDivisor(D, A, B)\\n+    [label(common-forward)]\\n+\\n+  claim <k> commonDivisor(D:Int, A:Int, B:Int) => true </k>\\n+    requires A >=Int 0 andBool B >Int 0 andBool D >=Int 0\\n+      andBool commonDivisor(D, B, pyMod(A, B))\\n+    [label(common-backward)]\\n+endmodule\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst a = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"kprove arith_spec.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module ARITH-SPEC --claims common-forward\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:12000});\ntext(a);\ntext(JSON.stringify(r));", "line": 197, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
