{"arguments": null, "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/spec.k\\n@@\\n module GCD-SPEC\\n   imports GCD-VERIFICATION\\n \\n+  // The submitted loop body implements one Euclidean transition under the\\n+  // unmodified reference rules.  This is the inductive step behind the\\n+  // symbolic loop summary in verification.k.\\n+  claim\\n+    <k> GcdLoopBody => .K </k>\\n+    <env> L:Int </env>\\n+    <scopes>\\n+      SC:Map\\n+      L |-> scope((\\\"a\\\" |-> A:Int\\n+                   \\\"b\\\" |-> B:Int), P:Parent)\\n+      => SC\\n+         L |-> scope((\\\"a\\\" |-> B\\n+                      \\\"b\\\" |-> pyMod(A, B)), P)\\n+    </scopes>\\n+    <heap> .Map </heap>\\n+    requires A >=Int 0 andBool B >Int 0\\n+    [label(euclid-step)]\\n+\\n   // For arbitrary signed integer arguments, the submitted function returns\\n*** Update File: /work/prove.sh\\n@@\\n # Universal symbolic theorem.\\n+kprove spec.k \\\\\\n+  --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+  --spec-module GCD-SPEC \\\\\\n+  --claims euclid-step \\\\\\n+  --warnings none\\n+\\n kprove spec.k \\\\\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst a = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"kprove spec.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module GCD-SPEC --claims euclid-step --warnings none\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:12000});\ntext(a);\ntext(JSON.stringify(r));", "line": 456, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
