{"arguments": null, "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/verification.k\\n@@\\n-  // Inductive loop summary used only when at least one loop-state component\\n-  // is symbolic.  Concrete executions continue through the unmodified MPY\\n-  // rules; the exact-value claims below therefore remain independent probes.\\n+  // Inductive loop summary for the Haskell proof definition.  It is absent\\n+  // from the separately compiled MPY-KRUN LLVM definition, whose executions\\n+  // therefore use only the supplied reference rules.\\n@@\\n     requires A >=Int 0 andBool B >=Int 0\\n     [priority(40), symbolic(A, B)]\\n-\\n-  // Zero-aware divisibility: 0 divides only 0.  This makes the standard\\n-  // divisibility characterization cover gcd(0, 0) = 0 without a partial mod.\\n-  syntax Bool ::= dividesZ(Int, Int) [function, total]\\n-  rule dividesZ(N:Int, N) => true\\n-    requires N >=Int 0\\n-    [simplification]\\n-  rule dividesZ(D:Int, 0) => true\\n-    requires D >=Int 0\\n-    [simplification]\\n-  rule dividesZ(0, N:Int) => N ==Int 0\\n-  rule dividesZ(D:Int, N:Int) => (N %Int D) ==Int 0\\n-    requires D =/=Int 0\\n-\\n-  syntax Bool ::= commonDivisor(Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\\n-  rule commonDivisor(D:Int, A:Int, B:Int) =>\\n-    dividesZ(D, A) andBool dividesZ(D, B)\\n endmodule\\n*** Update File: /work/spec.k\\n@@\\n-  // Prompt examples are proved directly with the reference semantics.  The\\n-  // symbolic loop summary is inapplicable because both loop locals are\\n-  // concrete, so these also guard the implementation/specification linkage.\\n+  // Prompt examples reduce gcdSpec through its concrete Euclidean equations;\\n+  // together with the separate MPY-KRUN run, they guard the abstraction and\\n+  // implementation/specification linkage at exact values.\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst a = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"./prove.sh > prove.log 2>&1\\nstatus=$?\\nprintf 'prove.sh exit: %s\\\\n' \\\"$status\\\"\\nrg -n '^#Top$|NoExc|<exit-code>|^[[:space:]]+0$' prove.log | tail -10\\nbash -n prove.sh\\npython3 py2mpy.py solution.py | cmp - solution.mpy\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:12000});\ntext(a);\ntext(JSON.stringify(r));", "line": 484, "message": null, "name": "exec", "phase": null, "type": "custom_tool_call"}
